WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.480
My turn!

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:29.920
I tribute Swordsman of Landstar to summon Jinzo!

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:33.240
Attack me.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.540
When you do, Chasm of Spikes will destroy it.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.950
Trap Crush!

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:43.770
What?

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:46.820
Too bad.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:51.860
As long as Jinzo is on the field, all your trap cards are destroyed.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:57.860
Courageous Gamble
Spin, Roulette Spider

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.440
This is bad.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:06.560
Jinzo has 2400 attack points.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.600
My monster has 1500 attack points.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:14.520
If it's destroyed, I lose 900 life points.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.120
I won't defeat you quickly.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.490
Next up is this!

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.420
The Equip Card Amplifier!

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.170
I equip it on Jinzo!

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.920
Jinzo gains 500 attack points!

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:37.670
It also gains 300 attack points every turn!

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:38.700
What?

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.370
Jinzo, attack!

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:44.020
Cyber Energy Shock!

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.360
Damn!

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:59.610
You attacked after raising its attack points with an Equip Card?

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.570
That's vile!

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.450
Hooray!

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.620
Yeah!  Nice, big bro!

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.380
Awesome!  Our big bro is really strong!

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:12.710
He's tough!

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.570
He's incredible!

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.750
Damn.  What should I do?

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.920
It's your turn, Jonouchi.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:30.430
You still have time to surrender.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:33.170
Surrender?  Whatever!

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.120
I'll never give up!

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:36.430
My turn!

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:40.360
Let me get a card that can turn this duel around!

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.880
Baby Dragon?

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.440
I'll use this to...

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.600
I don't have to use my ESP anymore.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:55.680
No matter what card you draw, you'll never destroy my Jinzo.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.920
You're finished on my next turn!

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:00.690
Are you sure?

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.850
I summon Baby Dragon!

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:10.250
Baby Dragon!

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:13.080
I know what Jonouchi is planning to do.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:18.250
You chose to summon Baby Dragon?

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:21.710
There's no way it can destroy my Jinzo!

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:23.820
Don't be so quick to judge.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:26.400
My turn isn't over yet.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:28.750
Time Wizard!

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:30.270
What?

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.700
I see.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:35.900
You're going to evolve Baby Dragon into Thousand Dragon.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:40.730
But my monster will still have more attack points than yours!

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.360
That's not Time Wizard's only effect.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:50.680
After a thousand years, even your precious Jinzo will rust into scrap metal.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.170
Here I go!  Time Roulette!

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:55.070
Time Roulette!

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:58.310
Hit the mark!

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:05.250
All right!

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:06.450
Time Magic!

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:10.060
Baby Dragon morphs into Thousand Dragon!

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:24.170
And a thousand years pass by, turning your Jinzo into scrap-

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.620
It didn't turn into scrap!

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:33.380
Why not?

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:38.430
Don't group it together with ordinary Machine-Type monsters.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:41.740
Jinzo's body is made of special alloys.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:45.480
No matter how many years pass by, it never rusts.

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.680
That's not fair!

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.910
You're done for!

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.400
Hang in there, Jonouchi.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:06:00.020
Jinzo, strike back at Thousand Dragon!

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:02.640
Cyber Energy Shock!

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:10.980
Even my Thousand Dragon was destroyed.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:13.920
Dammit.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:16.040
He was so close to winning.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:16.960
Honda?

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:18.990
How's my brother doing?

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:22.350
You said he was about to win.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:24.310
Umm, yeah...

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:28.070
He's not good at closing games out.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.930
So he's about to lose?

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.770
No, that's not it.

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:34.800
He'll definitely win next turn.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.160
Thank goodness.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.720
My brother always gets flustered in crucial situations.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:44.460
Honda?

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:48.580
Time to take your temperature.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:51.890
I'll wait outside until you're done.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.050
Thank you.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:55.900
See you later.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:00.500
Get your act together, Jonouchi.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.600
Shizuka is rooting for you.

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:09.620
Good.  You're getting better.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:11.720
Umm, nurse?

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:12.410
Yes?

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:16.810
Can you tell me who's winning the duel?

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:33.100
Guess who?

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:36.130
Grandpa!

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:40.210
Hey!  You shouldn't hurt the elderly!

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:43.200
Sheesh, you scared me!

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:47.620
Hello?

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:48.950
Hey, Honda!

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:51.600
Are you with Jonouchi?

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.420
Jonouchi?

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:54.680
I'm not with him.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.590
I need you to tell him something.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:07.100
What can you do with only one card in your hand?

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:09.260
You lose, Jonouchi.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:11.010
Give up!

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:17.000
Sorry, Roba.  "Giving up" isn't in my dictionary!

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:19.540
The spell card Scapegoat!

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:27.660
You're using Scapegoat to protect you?

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:31.650
That will only buy you a small amount of time.

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:37.670
Stop fighting back in vain and admit defeat, Jonouchi.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:44.520
Roba is right.

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:46.270
The duel is over.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:49.820
It's pointless to continue, Jonouchi.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.340
I end my turn!

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.920
Good, Jonouchi.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:56.940
Don't give up.

00:08:57.150 --> 00:09:00.810
There's always a way to open the doors of victory.

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:05.180
We're done.

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:06.320
Thanks.

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:13.140
Come in.

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:16.130
I wonder how Jonouchi is doing.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:19.040
Did I miss the moment he won?

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:21.810
That's enough.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:27.680
Thank you, Honda.  But you don't need to pretend anymore.

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:32.180
The nurse told me the truth.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:35.350
My brother is losing, right?

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:37.840
I'm sorry.

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:40.710
I didn't want you to worry.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:46.530
I understand, but I want to know the truth.

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:51.950
If my brother is fighting hard, then I want to cheer him on.

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:58.570
When I was wary of my operation, he cheered me on.

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:02.080
So it's my turn now!

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:06.200
I want to fight alongside him, even if it's only in spirit.

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:07.660
Shizuka...

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:11.160
But I'm happy that you care about me.

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:12.800
Thank you.

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:18.000
Let's cheer for Jonouchi together!

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:19.440
Okay!

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:43.510
If you're not giving up, that's fine.

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:45.790
I'll just thoroughly defeat you.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:48.600
My turn!

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:55.320
I summon Reflect Bounder!

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:05.570
Reflect Bounder reflects your attacking monster's attack points back one time.

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:11.980
In other words, even if you summon a monster, it won't be able to attack.

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:13.850
How dare you!

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:20.460
Due to Amplifier's effect, Jinzo gains 300 attack points.

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:26.640
Do you understand that you can't win?

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:29.240
Defeat is in your future!

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:36.000
Prepare yourself!

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.950
I attack with two monsters!

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:40.640
Cyber Energy Shock!

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:44.510
And Magic Mirror Beam!

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:55.900
Two Scapegoats are destroyed.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:00.300
You have two Scapegoats left.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:07.210
If I summon another monster next turn and attack with three monsters, you're finished!

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:10.540
It's frustrating, but he's right.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.770
My victory is certain!

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:15.550
There's no point continuing this duel!

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:17.780
Surrender!

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:23.150
Damn...

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:28.530
Jonouchi...

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:33.080
Admit your defeat and grovel before me, Jonouchi.

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:39.840
Sorry, Yugi.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:44.710
It seems I can't keep our promise.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:47.800
Shizuka is watching you!

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:51.310
Jonouchi!

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:53.150
Anzu...

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:55.570
Honda called me.

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:59.400
She's watching your duel on the internet.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:02.800
Honda is providing the play-by-play.

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:03.730
Honda?

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:08.720
So do your best, Jonouchi!

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:20.760
Shizuka, you fought your illness and won.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:26.330
So it's now my turn.

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:29.720
If you're watching, I can't look pathetic.

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:31.480
What's wrong?

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:33.190
Hurry up and surrender!

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:34.700
You must be joking!

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:35.810
What?

00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:39.030
He's fine.

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:42.050
Look at his eyes.

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:46.150
His eyes aren't dead yet.

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:52.670
Thanks to Shizuka, I remember that I still have one final card.

00:13:55.420 --> 00:14:00.140
My only chance is to draw it.

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:03.450
Jonouchi, believe in your cards!

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:06.050
Here I go!  My turn!

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:07.740
Yeah!

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:10.940
The spell card Roulette Spider!

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:17.970
What?

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:28.480
I'm making a last big gamble on my spell card Roulette Spider!

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:35.650
I have to pay half of my life points to play this card, but I don't care!

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:41.850
What are you going to do?

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:49.450
Roulette Spider blindfolds and spins the monster with the most attack points.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:53.540
It will attack the target that the arrow points to.

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:55.140
What?

00:14:55.370 --> 00:15:02.040
The targets are both players and all the monsters on the field.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:06.080
If it points to a player, he'll take big damage.

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:11.890
You're the one who'll stop the roulette, you psychic freak!

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:13.250
What?

00:15:14.570 --> 00:15:16.760
He uses crazy cards!

00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:20.060
Dice cards, Time Wizard...

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.760
It's a gamble deck that relies on luck.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:24.540
Here goes!

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:26.830
Spin, Roulette Spider!

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:28.310
Spinning.

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:39.650
Stop the arrow with your ESP!

00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:48.150
If it points at me, I'll take Jinzo's 3200 attack points!

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:03.540
What's wrong?

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:11.280
Stop!

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:25.100
The arrow is pointing at my Reflect Bounder.

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:26.320
That means...

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:35.070
Reflect it, Reflect Bounder!

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:44.010
It's no good!  It can't completely reflect Jinzo's 3200 attack points!

00:16:55.830 --> 00:17:00.390
Jinzo and Reflect Bounder are both destroyed!

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:04.070
They destroyed each other.

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:06.220
Impossible!

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:13.700
Jinzo has 3200 attack points, and Reflect Bounder has 1700.

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:17.910
You lose the difference, so you lose 1500 life points!

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:23.420
I win this duel!

00:17:23.710 --> 00:17:25.220
All right!

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:30.290
Yeah!  Jonouchi won!

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:33.060
You did it, big brother!

00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:39.060
He won by luck?

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:43.250
No, his tenacity brought him luck.

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:51.410
Big bro lost!

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:53.080
Dammit!

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:56.750
But it was a good duel.

00:17:57.820 --> 00:18:00.280
I lost?

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:03.040
Hey, Esper Roba lost.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:06.160
Against an amateur duelist who didn't know the rules.

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:10.000
I won.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:13.200
Hand over your rare card and Puzzle Card.

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:18.740
Everyone, stop looking down on me!

00:18:21.770 --> 00:18:25.660
Roba, I'm not looking down on you.

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:29.480
I was just lucky.

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:34.350
No one here is looking down on you.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:38.690
Be quiet!  You don't know anything!

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:41.130
Don't put pressure on yourself, Roba.

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:45.030
Dammit!  I'm not allowed to lose!

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:52.360
As long as I kept winning, everyone thought I was great!

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:53.770
Roba...

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:58.680
If everyone thought I was tough, no one would bully my brothers!

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:03.350
I protected my brothers by being great at this card game!

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:05.440
Stop whining!

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:09.040
In Battle City, you lose if you can't stand up!

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:11.360
Here.

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:13.920
Stand up.

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:15.790
Stop that!

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:19.080
I don't want pity!

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:21.680
Do whatever you want!

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:24.200
Stand up, big bro!

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:27.040
What's that voice?

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:29.480
Stand up!

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:31.600
Stand up, big bro!

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:40.120
You guys...

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:43.420
This is our final message.

00:19:45.170 --> 00:19:46.270
You guys...

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:48.660
Big bro!

00:19:50.740 --> 00:19:54.940
I'm sorry that I lost.

00:19:56.060 --> 00:19:57.040
It's fine.

00:19:57.040 --> 00:20:00.510
You were awesome when you dueled without cheating.

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:06.960
We'll be fine, so duel fair and square from now on!

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:07.950
Okay.

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:11.760
So that's how he "communicated with the universe."

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:14.450
I'm so moved emotionally!

00:20:17.030 --> 00:20:20.860
Jonouchi, I can't afford to lose either.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:31.100
My rare card and Puzzle Card.

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:32.940
Please take them.

00:20:33.570 --> 00:20:34.280
Okay.

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:37.510
Will you duel me again sometime?

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:39.570
Esper Roba...

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.980
I'm not an esper anymore.  I'm just Roba.

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:46.160
I won't cheat next time.

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:50.600
I'm looking forward to it.

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:54.560
Roba.

00:20:55.930 --> 00:20:58.130
You have brothers.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:02.630
I have a sister and irreplaceable friends.

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:06.300
A person who isn't alone is strong.

00:21:08.860 --> 00:21:09.900
See you.

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:12.930
Way to go, Jonouchi!

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:13.480
Yeah!

00:21:14.220 --> 00:21:15.980
I did it, Yugi.

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:27.650
I did it, Shizuka.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:45.950
Yugi wanders around Battle City in search of his lost memories.

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:49.520
Be careful!  A new Ghoul assassin is after you!

00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:54.550
Led to a basement, Dark Magician appears before Yugi!

00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:59.600
Yugi accepts Pandora's challenge to determine who is the true Dark Magician user.

00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:02.550
Wait a sec!  This Duel Ring is...

00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:06.160
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Dark Magician User
Pandora

00:22:06.160 --> 00:22:07.600
Duel, standby!

00:22:22.430 --> 00:22:26.930
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:27.730 --> 00:22:32.300
I feel like I've been here

00:22:32.840 --> 00:22:41.980
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:42.280 --> 00:22:53.490
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:56.360 --> 00:23:01.000
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:01.670 --> 00:23:06.270
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:11.380
Will never change

00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:16.650
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:17.280 --> 00:23:21.850
To be who I am

00:23:22.450 --> 00:23:27.090
I've kept searching for something

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:31.800
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:34.730
I learned that's the answer

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:41.840
From now until forever...
